WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.285 --> 00:00:16.587
When Zann awoke, he wasn't sure where he was.

2
00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:18.809
It was dark and a little chilly.

3
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.412
He rubbed his fingers together to create a light, but nothing happened.

4
00:00:23.053 --> 00:00:24.374
That made him wake up a little more.

5
00:00:25.134 --> 00:00:27.737
As soon as he looked around, though, he remembered he was in the Hollow.

6
00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:31.500
Darb, Perda, Gliss, and Zing were lying nearby.

7
00:00:32.172 --> 00:00:35.695
They'd all spent a cold, uncomfortable night sleeping on the hard ground.

8
00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:39.098
"Ugh," Perda mumbled as she woke up.

9
00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:40.459
"It's freezing!"

10
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.203
Indeed the predawn chill hung over the swamp like a damp blanket.

11
00:00:45.804 --> 00:00:49.947
Without thinking, Zann tried to conjure up a fire, but again nothing happened.

12
00:00:50.788 --> 00:00:54.571
"Right, magic doesn't work in the Hollow," he reminded himself.

13
00:00:55.312 --> 00:00:56.272
Perda rubbed her eyes.

14
00:00:56.293 --> 00:01:00.972
"Hey," she said, leaning over and poking Gliss.

15
00:01:00.992 --> 00:01:02.634
"Is that Darb's jacket?"

16
00:01:02.654 --> 00:01:05.916
"Yeah." Darb sat up and stretched.

17
00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:10.020
"Gliss was shivering last night, and I figured she needed it more than I did."

18
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.102
That was just like Darb.

19
00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:15.605
He was always willing to give up his own comfort to help someone else.

20
00:01:16.345 --> 00:01:18.827
Usually it was one of the things Zann liked about his friend.

21
00:01:19.468 --> 00:01:21.770
But today for some reason it annoyed Zann a little.

22
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:28.335
"Nice of you to offer the jacket to the rest of us," Perda told Darb sarcastically, obviously feeling

23
00:01:28.355 --> 00:01:28.916
the same way.

24
00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:32.654
Darb didn't say anything, but Gliss sat up and looked at Perda.

25
00:01:32.674 --> 00:01:35.236
"Sorry," she said quickly.

26
00:01:35.256 --> 00:01:37.417
"I didn't ask him to give it to me.

27
00:01:38.178 --> 00:01:41.060
Anyway, you guys are the ones who talked me into staying out here."

28
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.842
"What else are we supposed to do?"

29
00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:44.842
Zann said.

30
00:01:44.862 --> 00:01:49.325
"Do you want to go sit in your house all alone and wait for Morb to come grab

31
00:01:49.345 --> 00:01:52.047
you?" As soon as he said it, he regretted it.

32
00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:55.269
Gliss' face fell and a tear ran down her cheek.

33
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.151
Perda scowled at Zann.

34
00:01:57.351 --> 00:01:58.672
"That wasn't very nice."

35
00:01:59.596 --> 00:02:01.057
"Sorry," Zann muttered.

36
00:02:01.077 --> 00:02:03.319
"What are we going to do?"

37
00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:05.180
Gliss asked in a shaky voice.

38
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.443
"Morb blasted through my parents' Shield spell like it was nothing."

39
00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:13.266
"We've got to look for Boz's diary," Darb said.

40
00:02:13.286 --> 00:02:14.887
"And then what?"

41
00:02:15.247 --> 00:02:15.847
Gliss asked.

42
00:02:16.588 --> 00:02:21.351
"Even if the diary survived the explosion, how are we supposed to get it to the palace?

43
00:02:22.192 --> 00:02:24.834
First City is halfway across Magica!"

44
00:02:24.854 --> 00:02:27.155
"Why don't we take it to the mayor?"

45
00:02:27.415 --> 00:02:28.156
Darb suggested.

46
00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.721
"Maybe she'll know what to do."

47
00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:32.923
Gliss nodded, looking hopeful for the first time.

48
00:02:32.943 --> 00:02:37.246
"Everyone says the mayor is the most powerful Red in Swamp Bottom."

49
00:02:38.027 --> 00:02:39.428
She shot a glance at Zann.

50
00:02:39.448 --> 00:02:41.569
"Well, except for Boz.

51
00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.810
But he's retired."

52
00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.672
"And missing," Perda pointed out.

53
00:02:45.692 --> 00:02:48.114
"I think you're right about the mayor, Darb.

54
00:02:48.454 --> 00:02:50.015
She can help us if anyone can."

55
00:02:50.756 --> 00:02:51.516
Zann shrugged.

56
00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:53.318
He was ready to get out of the Hollow.

57
00:02:53.338 --> 00:02:56.400
"Let's worry about all that later," he said.

58
00:02:57.144 --> 00:02:59.125
"First we need to find that diary."

59
00:03:03.587 --> 00:03:05.728
Morb glared at the old woman facing him.

60
00:03:06.368 --> 00:03:08.349
Her sunken eyes burned with disdain.

61
00:03:08.369 --> 00:03:12.711
"Why did you come today if you're not going to help me?"

62
00:03:13.111 --> 00:03:13.671
he demanded.

63
00:03:13.691 --> 00:03:18.813
"I can't help you anymore," she croaked in a deep, dark voice.

64
00:03:19.713 --> 00:03:21.814
"What you are doing is too much.

65
00:03:22.575 --> 00:03:27.061
When we made our deal, I never intended—" "That's enough!"

66
00:03:27.481 --> 00:03:28.161
Morb thundered.

67
00:03:28.181 --> 00:03:31.723
"Who are you to lecture me about right and wrong?

68
00:03:32.443 --> 00:03:33.724
You're no better than I am."

69
00:03:34.725 --> 00:03:36.285
The old woman's eyes narrowed.

70
00:03:36.946 --> 00:03:40.308
"Perhaps not," she said in a low, ominous voice.

71
00:03:40.328 --> 00:03:47.511
"But I have lived many years and seen many things, including the downfall of others who tried to

72
00:03:47.571 --> 00:03:49.853
do more than their destinies allowed."

73
00:03:49.873 --> 00:03:54.275
"I believe in making my own destiny," Morb retorted.

74
00:03:54.935 --> 00:03:55.916
The woman shook her head.

75
00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:58.369
"Making your own destiny?"

76
00:03:58.749 --> 00:03:59.109
she said.

77
00:03:59.129 --> 00:04:01.149
"Or stealing it?"

78
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.850
Morb's face twisted with anger.

79
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:09.752
Ready to send a Blast spell flying, he rubbed his fingers together; the friction made a crackling sound.

80
00:04:10.532 --> 00:04:14.513
"You know better than that," the old woman said with a slight smile.

81
00:04:15.353 --> 00:04:18.634
"Like it or not, you still need me, Morb."

82
00:04:19.374 --> 00:04:20.575
Morb lowered his hand.

83
00:04:20.935 --> 00:04:22.395
"Perhaps," he said.

84
00:04:22.415 --> 00:04:24.836
"But not for much longer."

85
00:04:25.612 --> 00:04:27.873
For the first time, the old woman looked worried.

86
00:04:27.893 --> 00:04:29.593
"What do you mean?

87
00:04:29.953 --> 00:04:35.695
Without my help you could never—" "I'm tired of this conversation," Morb interrupted loudly.

88
00:04:36.535 --> 00:04:40.256
He'd just noticed a swarm of flizzes zipping in through the window.

89
00:04:40.276 --> 00:04:48.218
"Leave." The old woman hesitated, her deep-set eyes studying Morb's face with a mix of curiosity and dread.

90
00:04:48.998 --> 00:04:51.499
Slowly she turned and walked out of the room.

91
00:04:52.159 --> 00:04:54.880
When she was gone, Morb stepped toward the flizzes.

92
00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.922
"What have you brought me, my pretties?"

93
00:04:58.462 --> 00:04:58.922
he asked.

94
00:04:59.703 --> 00:05:03.305
Several of the tiny dragons were struggling to carry pieces of paper.

95
00:05:04.046 --> 00:05:06.087
Morb grabbed the papers and examined them.

96
00:05:06.808 --> 00:05:09.229
A smile spread across his thin face.

97
00:05:09.249 --> 00:05:11.411
"Perfect," he said.

98
00:05:11.431 --> 00:05:14.173
"You've done well, my tiny friends."

99
00:05:15.053 --> 00:05:19.776
Striding over to the Secret Eye, he paused and glanced at the map image hovering above it.

100
00:05:20.717 --> 00:05:23.539
It was still blank, with no red dots visible at all.

101
00:05:24.379 --> 00:05:24.840
Never mind.

102
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.121
The boy couldn't resist using magic forever.

103
00:05:27.781 --> 00:05:30.282
As soon as Zann slipped, Morb would be ready.

104
00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.264
He looked once more at the blink images in his hand.

105
00:05:34.324 --> 00:05:37.745
One showed the Red girl whose parents now languished in one of his cells.

106
00:05:38.386 --> 00:05:41.687
The other picture was of the tall non-Red who had been with the others.

107
00:05:42.828 --> 00:05:47.710
Morb stuffed both images into the Secret Eye alongside the blink image of Boz's grandson.

108
00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.090
Nothing happened.

109
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.091
No red dots appeared on the map.

110
00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:52.692
Morb scowled.

111
00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:57.692
He didn't have time to stand here waiting for those foolish children to use magic.

112
00:05:58.472 --> 00:06:01.515
His plans were underway, and there was still much to do.

113
00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.696
He summoned several trolls.

114
00:06:03.716 --> 00:06:05.398
"Watch the map!"

115
00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:06.318
he ordered them.

116
00:06:06.338 --> 00:06:12.443
"As soon as it shows the location of the young fugitives, seize them and bring them to me."
